        "summary": "dc χMT at 300 K is 47.12 cm3 K mol−1 (expected 47.28 for six uncoupled GdIII). χMT decreases to 13.22 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, indicating antiferromagnetic Gd···Gd coupling. Curie–Weiss fit (50–300 K) gives C = 49.33 cm3 mol−1 K and θ = −14.11 K. No out-of-phase ac peaks, so no SMM behavior above 2 K. Solid-state emission (λex = 370 nm) shows ligand fluorescence at 395, 421, and 470 nm.",
