        "summary": "χMT at 300 K is 83.82 cm3 K mol−1 (expected 85.02 for six uncoupled DyIII), remains roughly constant to 14 K, then drops to 72.04 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Curie–Weiss fit (50–300 K): C = 83.53 cm3 mol−1 K, θ = 1.06 K. Magnetization reaches 31.74 Nβ at 2 K and 50 kOe (below 60 Nβ saturation). Zero-dc-field ac data (0.4–15 K) are frequency-dependent; χ″ peaks near 2 K indicate SMM behavior (φ = 0.28). Arrhenius fit gives Ueff = 7.6 K and τ0 = 1.1×10−6 s; a second χ″ process appears near 6 K. Solid-state emission shows one peak at 476 nm assigned to DyIII 4F9/2 → 6H15/2.",
